# The Paper 9 package must stay byte-identical to the archive published with the
# paper: paper9/MANIFEST_SHA256.txt hashes every file, and
# reproduce_clusters.py compares its generated Table 2 byte-for-byte against
# expected/table2_seven.csv, which is deliberately CRLF so the comparison holds
# on any OS. Line-ending conversion would break both.
paper9/** -text

# The Paper 10 package hashes its files byte for byte: reproduce.py checks the
# SHA-256 of the shipped data tables, and file_manifest.csv lists the SHA-256 of
# every file. Line-ending conversion would break both.
paper10/** -text

# The Paper 8 package hashes its files byte for byte (paper8/MANIFEST_SHA256.txt), and
# reproduce.py checks the SHA-256 of the shipped CSV files. Line-ending conversion would
# break both.
paper8/** -text

# The Paper 7 package hashes its files byte for byte (paper7/MANIFEST_SHA256.txt and
# paper7/file_manifest.csv), and reproduce.py checks the SHA-256 of the board, its
# Corbelli input table, the kernel, the age lock and the canonical-gate predictions.
# Line-ending conversion would break all three.
paper7/** -text
